[Cursor Rules]
Use the real FlareMo auth integration points instead of inventing a second password-reset stack. Self-service reset is POST /api/auth/flaremo/forgot-password plus Better Auth emailAndPassword.sendResetPassword; both send mail through sendPasswordResetEmail. The reset page posts to Better Auth /api/auth/reset-password.
Do not put RESEND_API_KEY, BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, or FLAREMO_BOOTSTRAP_SECRET in git or PR bodies. Mail keys stay as Worker secrets via wrangler secret put.
Do not implement FLAREMO_RECOVERY_SECRET as the user-facing forgot-password path when Resend is the chosen recovery option.
Nothing deploys on push. There is no deploy workflow; the live site changes only through scripts/fork/prod-deploy.mjs (see docs/fork-dev-environment.md).

[Knowledge Learned]
Forgot-password stays off until FLAREMO_EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend, FLAREMO_EMAIL_FROM, and Worker secret RESEND_API_KEY are set.
Better Auth only calls sendResetPassword for an existing user. Throwing from that hook would 500 known addresses and 200 unknown ones, which enumerates accounts. Delivery failures stay logged inside sendPasswordResetEmail.
revokeSessionsOnPasswordReset invalidates cookie sessions. memos_pat_ tokens survive self-service reset. Operator /recover still revokes sessions and PATs. Do not invent a new revocation policy without stating it.
Wrangler deploy preserves existing Worker secrets.

[Project Styles]
Deployment and auth docs exist in docs/deploy.md and docs/en/deploy.md; keep the secret-name tables in both.
Worker public flags are wrangler vars (FLAREMO_EMAIL_PROVIDER, FLAREMO_EMAIL_FROM). API keys are wrangler secrets.
Auth pages use AuthPageFrame plus existing i18n keys; do not add unimplemented recovery UI.
